GAL22V10
UA6RHHD

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =====================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  -  HD-ONLY bring-up  (RAM DISABLED, no SIMMs)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; *** REVISED per RH800C USER MANUAL (RocHard_RH800C.pdf) ***
; The manual DOCUMENTS running the HDD with ZERO RAM (DIP-2 OFF, no
; SIMMs, no strap). Therefore HD autoconfig must NOT depend on any RAM
; strap. So /_DRVEN here is derived WITHOUT /_GALSTROBE (which is UA4's
; strap-gated RAM-path signal). This corrects the earlier draft that
; gated /_DRVEN on /_GALSTROBE and thus wrongly required RAM.
;
; Netlist-confirmed facts this build relies on:
;   * /_E8WIN (UA4.23) can only go low when /_DRVEN (UA4.14) is low
;     AND /_BANK_SEL is low. UA4 is a pure slave of /_DRVEN. So /_DRVEN
;     is UA6's one autoconfig-critical output.
;   * The autoconfig ID (er_Type = 0xC1: Zorro II, MEMLIST CLEAR) is
;     served by the BOOT ROM (U6/U20) on /DB12-15. UA6 leaves DB12-15
;     Hi-Z -> ROM supplies the controller identity -> no MEMLIST -> OS
;     adds NO memory board -> no $200000 probe -> no fast-RAM hang.
;   * Base/window decode = U9/U10/U11 + RN1/RN2 (original chips), NOT
;     UA6. UA6 is not a base latch.
;   * /_AC_PHASE (UA6.16 -> U11.5): U11's crack shows i5 unused, but a
;     FLOATING U11.5 is dangerous; original black-box showed this pin
;     driven LOW, so we match that. TUNABLE.
;
; BOARD SETTINGS for HD-only-no-RAM (per manual + UA4 equations):
;   Game switch  = II   (grounds /_BANK_SEL -> lets /_E8WIN open)
;   DIP-1 (HDD)  = ON   (firmware HDD-enable via /HDEN/U17)
;   DIP-2 (RAM)  = OFF  (RAM disabled; no strap asserted - fine now)
;   DIP-3        = per Kickstart version (OFF=1.3+, ON=1.2)
;   SIMMs        = none required
; =====================================================================


; ---- /_DRVEN (pin 23) : master enable, LATCHED. STRAP-INDEPENDENT.
; Keeps /_E8WIN STABLY low so U10 stays enabled and /_CFGADDR_MATCH
; fires during the $E8 read. With the ORIGINAL U14 (correct polarity:
; _ROMOE HIGH default, LOW on match), the match ENABLES the ROM during
; the ID read -> U6 serves the ID + U11 selects the card + DTACKs.
;   HISTORY: the earlier "_ROMOE high on match -> ROM starved" that made
;   me add a write-gate was a CLONE U14 with INVERTED _ROMOE polarity
;   (bad crack). Original U14 back in 2026-07-21 -> _ROMOE HIGH default,
;   goes LOW on the match = ROM on during the config read. So the latch
;   (U10 matching through the reads) is now CORRECT; the write-gate was
;   compensating for the wrong chip.
; NO /_GALSTROBE term (strap-free).
/DRVEN = /CFGIN & /BASEA & RST
       + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RST


; ---- /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) -> U11.5 : LEAVE UNDRIVEN (Hi-Z) -----------
; IN-CIRCUIT 2026-07-21: driving this pin LOW RED-SCREENED the Amiga
; (it was the only actively-driven UA6 output; /_DRVEN wasn't even
; asserting). The clean-booting ua6_rebuild left this pin floating, so
; revert to that: Hi-Z. (The original chip read out LOW here, but the
; original is the suspected-broken part - matching it matched the fault.)
ACPHASE.T = VCC
ACPHASE.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- DB12-15 (pins 18-21) : permanent Hi-Z --------------------------
; Let the boot ROM (U6/U20) drive er_Type (0xC1 controller, MEMLIST
; clear). .E forced false via a tautological contradiction.
DB15.T = VCC
DB15.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB14.T = VCC
DB14.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB13.T = VCC
DB13.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB12.T = VCC
DB12.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- NC15 (pin 15), NC22 (pin 22) : unconnected pads, force Hi-Z -----
NC15.T = VCC
NC15.E = AB1 & /AB1
NC22.T = VCC
NC22.E = AB1 & /AB1


DESCRIPTION

UA6 HD-only bring-up for RocHard RH800C (RAM disabled).

REVISED per the RH800C user manual, which documents HDD operation with
zero RAM. /_DRVEN is derived independent of any RAM strap (NO /_GALSTROBE
term). UA6's job reduces to: assert /_DRVEN so UA4 can pull /_E8WIN low
(enabling U10's window compare and U11's DTACK), while leaving DB12-15
Hi-Z so the boot ROM supplies the controller er_Type - RAM is never
announced, so the OS never probes $200000.

STILL A RECONSTRUCTION - open question: exactly how the $E8 autoconfig
window is decoded without /_GALSTROBE (likely U10/U14/ROM-enable, not
UA6). This /_DRVEN is a "card-enabled latch" first cut; the original's
internal state pins (15/22) may sequence it more precisely.

WATCH ON TEST (probe, in order):
  1. /_BANK_SEL (UA4.20)   - LOW (game switch II).
  2. /_DRVEN (UA6.23 / UA4.14) - goes LOW and stays low after first access.
  3. /_E8WIN (UA4.23)      - should then drop and stay low; U10 enabled.
Expected in DiagROM: ONE Zorro II board, mfr 2144, prod 1; NO memory
board, no $200000 hang. Board set to: game II, DIP-1 ON, DIP-2 OFF.
